1
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,120
(Episode 80)

2
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:04,750
Han Su Cheol?

3
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,590
This can't be.

4
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:10,430
Dad...

5
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:14,060
Dad did this to Gyeol's father...

6
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:19,970
Seung Ri.

7
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:23,270
Dad.

8
00:00:24,070 --> 00:00:26,740
Victim Han Su Cheol.

9
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:31,680
Don't tell me he's Gyeol's biological father.

10
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:36,390
That's not true, right?

11
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:38,720
Right, Dad?

12
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:42,690
Say it isn't true. Please, just say it isn't true.

13
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:46,900
Seung Ri.

14
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:48,700
I'm so sorry.

15
00:00:49,730 --> 00:00:50,730
I'm just so sorry.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,700
So it's true?

17
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,740
The person you killed in that accident...

18
00:00:58,010 --> 00:01:00,940
was really Gyeol's biological father?

19
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:05,080
I'm sorry.

20
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:07,220
I'm so sorry.

21
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:12,220
No. How could this happen?

22
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:14,520
How could you, for all this time,

23
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,390
act so normal in front of Gyeol?

24
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,730
He trusted and relied on you so much.

25
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:22,300
Calm down, Seung Ri. Please.

26
00:01:23,970 --> 00:01:24,970
Let go of me.

27
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,340
You're scaring me, Dad. You're giving me the creeps.

28
00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:34,210
All those times I said I liked Gyeol,

29
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:37,650
what in the world were you thinking when you looked at me?

30
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:40,180
Dad, are you really my father?

31
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,550
Are you really the dad...

32
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:46,420
I respected and loved most?

33
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,330
Yes.

34
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:53,930
I know nothing can excuse what I did,

35
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,400
but I wanted to protect our family.

36
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:02,240
But my wrong choice led to this.

37
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:07,940
For our family? Does that even make sense?

38
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:11,250
Because of you, Gyeol lost everything.

39
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:14,650
Seung Ri, I'm sorry.

40
00:02:18,350 --> 00:02:19,360
Seung Ri.

41
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:25,160
Why did you come back?

42
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:29,100
What? I forgot to take the documents wit me.

43
00:02:29,670 --> 00:02:30,670
I'm just leaving.

44
00:02:36,070 --> 00:02:38,140
Is that Seung Ri I hear?

45
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:45,950
Seo Seung Ri.

46
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:48,450
When did you get back?

47
00:02:53,190 --> 00:02:54,690
Did something happen at work?

48
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,230
Say something.

49
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:02,470
I'm not feeling well.

50
00:03:02,970 --> 00:03:05,170
Just let me be alone. I'm begging you.

51
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:07,340
Where does it hurt? Why are you crying?

52
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:08,810
Get up right now.

53
00:03:09,070 --> 00:03:10,440
If you're sick, you should go to the hospital.

54
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:14,140
This isn't about Gyeol, is it?

55
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,880
It can't be, right?

56
00:03:16,410 --> 00:03:18,250
Mom, please.

57
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:22,090
All right. Get some rest for now.

58
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:40,400
She said she came home because she wasn't feeling well.

59
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:42,340
Do you know what happened?

60
00:03:44,770 --> 00:03:46,410
Please stay with her and take good care of her.

61
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,510
I should get going.

62
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:52,320
What is going on?

63
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:55,080
You and your daughter are both so tight-lipped.

64
00:03:55,550 --> 00:03:57,550
Are you trying to drive me crazy?

65
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:03,660
Did something happen, sir? Your face...

66
00:04:04,890 --> 00:04:05,999
It's nothing. I was drinking...

67
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,300
and bumped into something. Forget it.

68
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,370
Should I get you some ointment?

69
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
No. Is this what they call...

70
00:04:12,070 --> 00:04:13,200
hurting someone then offering to help?

71
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:17,270
Did you leak it by any chance?

72
00:04:17,510 --> 00:04:21,810
- Sir? Leak what? - The Chief Financial Officer...

73
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:24,080
No, it's nothing. Forget it. It's nothing at all.

74
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:25,450
Leave. Go on.

75
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,750
Yes, sir.

76
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:30,990
Oh, hello.

77
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,560
Father, here are some clean clothes for you.

78
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:38,530
Why did you leave the house without even changing?

79
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:41,600
Well, I was drinking in my study and fell asleep for a bit,

80
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:43,470
and I had an early meeting, so I just left as I was.

81
00:04:44,470 --> 00:04:47,370
By the way, did Grandfather say anything?

82
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:50,570
No. Grandmother told him you had a breakfast meeting...

83
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:53,240
and left very early, so he didn't say anything.

84
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,910
- Grandmother did? - Yes.

85
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,080
But it seems you didn't have...

86
00:04:59,150 --> 00:05:01,480
a breakfast meeting. So what happened?

87
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:04,020
Wait, hold on.

88
00:05:04,490 --> 00:05:05,920
Did you get into a fight with someone?

89
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:09,190
Oh, forget it. Just leave. Quickly.

90
00:05:09,890 --> 00:05:10,890
Oh, okay.

91
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,270
Crystal, honestly.

92
00:05:17,770 --> 00:05:19,140
She must be making a big deal out of this.

93
00:05:24,810 --> 00:05:25,840
Honey, where are you right now?

94
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:28,880
- Where else? I'm at the office. - Are you sure you're at the office?

95
00:05:29,150 --> 00:05:30,180
Then let's video chat.

96
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,980
A video call? What are you talking about? Min Ho just left.

97
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,080
Go ahead, ask Min Ho where I am.

98
00:05:35,490 --> 00:05:38,960
Really? And you have a clear conscience?

99
00:05:39,490 --> 00:05:43,630
Come on, Crystal. If you don't believe me, who will?

100
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:47,560
If you can't trust a devoted man like me, who can you trust?

101
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:51,230
Oh, that's right. My darling only has eyes for me.

102
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:54,070
Okay, honey. Come home early tonight.

103
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:55,610
Oh, hey, Crystal.

104
00:05:56,110 --> 00:05:57,110
By the way,

105
00:05:57,170 --> 00:05:59,140
did Chief Seo come to the house this morning?

106
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:02,350
Chief Seo? No, he didn't come in today.

107
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:04,910
Right. Okay, I'm hanging up.

108
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,680
Hold on.

109
00:06:09,290 --> 00:06:10,490
Seo Gwon Sik, that jerk...

110
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:13,160
He's not getting any funny ideas, is he?

111
00:06:15,690 --> 00:06:18,900
Honestly, why is he always so worried about Chief Seo?

112
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:21,600
Now that the search for Mother's daughter is over,

113
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:24,070
he'll soon be powerless anyway. Why all the fuss?

114
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:25,900
What? Seung Ri?

115
00:06:26,470 --> 00:06:27,540
How sick is she?

116
00:06:28,470 --> 00:06:29,470
Oh, I see.

117
00:06:29,770 --> 00:06:32,409
Okay, I'll finish something urgent...

118
00:06:32,410 --> 00:06:33,640
and get there as fast as I can.

119
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:35,780
Okay. Yes.

120
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:39,520
I wonder what's wrong.

121
00:06:44,850 --> 00:06:47,060
Why isn't Manager Seo here yet?

122
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:51,230
She came in this morning. I rode the elevator with her.

123
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:53,330
What? Then why isn't she here?

124
00:06:54,230 --> 00:06:55,700
Maybe she had to go straight to a client meeting?

125
00:06:56,830 --> 00:06:59,470
Manager Seo felt unwell today,

126
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:01,470
so she came in briefly and then went home early.

127
00:07:01,770 --> 00:07:04,410
- We'll meet as a team tomorrow. - Okay.

128
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:05,910
Is she really unwell?

129
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:09,880
Oh, I think it's just a bug. Don't worry too much.

130
00:07:09,950 --> 00:07:11,610
All right, everyone, keep up the good work.

131
00:07:17,290 --> 00:07:18,850
The materials are ready, Team Leader Ko.

132
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,220
Okay, let's start the meeting in ten minutes.

133
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,500
I've updated the date course recommendation feature.

134
00:07:30,570 --> 00:07:33,570
It considers users' health and travel distance...

135
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:37,110
- to recommend courses on its own. - I see.

136
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:38,770
For cultural experiences,

137
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:40,940
I think programs like performances, exhibitions,

138
00:07:41,010 --> 00:07:42,210
and workshops would be good.

139
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,480
So I'm currently compiling the materials.

140
00:07:43,550 --> 00:07:44,649
Thanks to your hard work,

141
00:07:44,650 --> 00:07:46,320
the forecast for this competition looks good.

142
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:49,490
Seeing Grandfather's living funeral gave me an idea.

143
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:52,560
For any residents who might be interested,

144
00:07:52,690 --> 00:07:55,060
what if we offered to support them in holding a living funeral?

145
00:07:55,990 --> 00:07:58,860
A living funeral is meaningful,

146
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:00,330
but I'm a little concerned about...

147
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,470
how the residents will actually take it.

148
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,800
Let's run a preliminary survey...

149
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:08,270
- and discuss it again afterward. - Okay.

150
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:10,369
Excuse me, I have to take this.

151
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:11,410
- Okay. - Okay.

152
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,440
You know we have to clock out on the dot, right?

153
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,980
Clocking out on the dot?

154
00:08:17,910 --> 00:08:20,150
When I first said that, you didn't understand...

155
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:21,650
and asked me, "What's that?"

156
00:08:22,590 --> 00:08:24,050
I posted in the family group chat...

157
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:25,960
that we're taking care of dinner tonight.

158
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:29,630
A family group chat? We have one of those?

159
00:08:29,690 --> 00:08:33,500
Of course. We all need to see general announcements together.

160
00:08:34,530 --> 00:08:39,300
I'm hurt. You didn't even invite me. So much for being family.

161
00:08:40,170 --> 00:08:41,840
What? Are you sulking?

162
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:45,240
All right, I'll invite you now.

163
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:56,750
- Get inside, now. You're grounded. - Mom, come on.

164
00:08:56,950 --> 00:08:58,420
No matter how much the world has changed,

165
00:08:58,490 --> 00:08:59,960
what parent would let her grown daughter...

166
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:01,560
spend the night in a room alone with a man?

167
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:04,830
What parent would just stand by and watch? Get inside.

168
00:09:04,890 --> 00:09:05,900
Seriously.

169
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,500
- What's wrong? - I swear, I can't take it.

170
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:10,200
Did Eun Nim cause trouble again?

171
00:09:11,170 --> 00:09:12,170
I mean...

172
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:15,600
it's not like I'm asking for much.

173
00:09:16,210 --> 00:09:20,380
The guy is so cute and pretty.

174
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,610
Now you're just nitpicking.

175
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:25,750
- Right. That's unjustified bashing. - Unjustified bashing?

176
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:29,420
- It means unfair criticism. - And then there's his job.

177
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:32,020
I'm already upset that Eun Nim quit medical school...

178
00:09:32,090 --> 00:09:33,560
to write web novels or whatever,

179
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:36,330
and now her boyfriend writes webtoons for a living too.

180
00:09:36,390 --> 00:09:37,560
They do the same work.

181
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:41,000
Eun Nim's novels are really popular these days. Didn't you know?

182
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:43,400
She probably earns more than Eun Ae now.

183
00:09:43,470 --> 00:09:45,300
What? Eun Nim is doing that well?

184
00:09:46,470 --> 00:09:50,240
No, it's not about the money.

185
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:54,840
She should be out in the world, meeting lots of people,

186
00:09:55,010 --> 00:09:59,550
but she's cooped up in a tiny room, and the only person she sees is him.

187
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:02,219
Mother, it's Eun Nim's life.

188
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:04,050
If she's happy, that's all that matters.

189
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:06,760
Still, that's not how a parent feels.

190
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:11,390
I have clear standards...

191
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:14,530
for who can marry my granddaughter.

192
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:16,200
If I don't approve of him,

193
00:10:16,270 --> 00:10:18,900
I'll oppose the marriage at once.

194
00:10:19,370 --> 00:10:22,170
What are your deal-breakers for a grandson-in-law?

195
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:26,440
Well, there's, you know... A gambler, a loafer,

196
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,910
and a violent thug. Absolutely not.

197
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:30,780
Oh, Grandma.

198
00:10:30,850 --> 00:10:33,380
As if I would ever marry someone like that.

199
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:37,220
- Seriously. - One more is a single dad.

200
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:39,690
- What? - A single dad.

201
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:42,560
Even if he were the rich heir to a conglomerate,

202
00:10:42,630 --> 00:10:45,090
I'd oppose it completely. Remember that.

203
00:10:45,290 --> 00:10:46,300
Seriously.

204
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:48,600
I'm the one getting married, not you.

205
00:10:49,930 --> 00:10:51,900
I should get going.

206
00:10:52,170 --> 00:10:54,340
- Have a good day. - What?

207
00:10:56,410 --> 00:11:00,040
Grandma, how could you say that so bluntly?

208
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:01,640
What did I do?

209
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:05,480
A single dad? For her to hear that...

210
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:07,220
You don't think...

211
00:11:07,550 --> 00:11:10,650
she thought I was talking about Eun Hyung?

212
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:14,190
What do I do?

213
00:11:15,060 --> 00:11:18,190
(Grandma Pancake)

214
00:11:18,330 --> 00:11:19,560
A single dad?

215
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:22,500
Surely she wasn't talking about my Eun Hyung.

216
00:11:24,570 --> 00:11:28,670
Anyway, I hope Ji Seon changes her mind, even now.

217
00:11:33,110 --> 00:11:34,510
How have you been?

218
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:37,910
Time has flown by without me even realising it.

219
00:11:38,550 --> 00:11:39,550
I've been so busy.

220
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,690
Flying long-haul routes.

221
00:11:43,450 --> 00:11:45,890
Going to the police station whenever I had a free moment.

222
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:49,660
I was focused on paying off the debt as quickly as possible.

223
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:53,260
When you first asked for a divorce, Ji Seon,

224
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,700
I just couldn't understand it.

225
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,500
To think you'd get a divorce over 50,000 dollars...

226
00:12:00,070 --> 00:12:01,070
Right.

227
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,410
That's what everyone said.

228
00:12:04,070 --> 00:12:07,180
How could you leave your child behind...

229
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,710
and get a divorce over some measly money?

230
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,080
But...

231
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:17,220
I was really going through a lot back then.

232
00:12:19,020 --> 00:12:20,990
You had no grasp of reality,

233
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:24,560
and I was sick of fighting about money every day.

234
00:12:25,390 --> 00:12:27,230
I was backed into a corner and even got scammed,

235
00:12:27,730 --> 00:12:30,770
and then I lost what little money we had left.

236
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:35,070
I just couldn't forgive myself.

237
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:37,610
- Ji Seon... - When parents...

238
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:39,440
are struggling with money,

239
00:12:40,540 --> 00:12:43,110
their kids start walking on eggshells around them.

240
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:46,250
Even when they're struggling with money,

241
00:12:46,550 --> 00:12:48,720
it would be one thing if the couple was happy.

242
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:51,850
But we weren't like that.

243
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:58,090
You know my family's finances.

244
00:12:59,330 --> 00:13:01,200
I was afraid Bit Na would grow up...

245
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:02,530
with me always harping on money...

246
00:13:05,570 --> 00:13:09,000
and become obsessed with it herself.

247
00:13:10,570 --> 00:13:13,310
It's all my fault. It's because I wasn't good enough.

248
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:15,640
I'm not saying this to make you blame yourself.

249
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,910
Other than your lack of a grasp on reality,

250
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:24,320
you're the best father in the world and a wonderful husband.

251
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,660
Well, thank you for saying that.

252
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:36,170
Our cooling-off period is almost over.

253
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,600
Time flies.

254
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:41,640
It does.

255
00:13:44,010 --> 00:13:45,540
What are you going to do now?

256
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:49,910
What choice do I have?

257
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:53,950
Bit Na and I struggled at first,

258
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:55,920
but we're much more stable now.

259
00:13:57,050 --> 00:13:59,420
So don't worry too much about me and Bit Na.

260
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:02,120
From now on, think of this...

261
00:14:02,190 --> 00:14:03,890
as rewriting the first page of your own life.

262
00:14:04,890 --> 00:14:06,360
I'll be sincerely rooting for you.

263
00:14:13,570 --> 00:14:16,240
You have your regular check-up next week, right?

264
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:17,440
How are you feeling?

265
00:14:17,810 --> 00:14:19,440
Couldn't be better.

266
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:23,750
I was just nervous that day, so I seemed weak.

267
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:25,150
Oh, don't worry.

268
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:28,880
At this rate, I'll easily make it another year.

269
00:14:29,990 --> 00:14:31,750
Only one more year?

270
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:35,990
You can't just "make it." You need to get much better.

271
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,960
That's asking for too much.

272
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:41,800
These days, I really...

273
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:45,330
feel so grateful for each and every day.

274
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:49,240
You found Yeon Soon, which was your lifelong wish.

275
00:14:49,810 --> 00:14:51,210
And Min Ho and Gyeol...

276
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:55,680
finally seem to understand what I want and are getting along.

277
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,480
This matter...

278
00:14:59,650 --> 00:15:00,650
Hey.

279
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,350
Are you going somewhere?

280
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:05,090
Yes, I was thinking of dropping by Seung Ri's place.

281
00:15:05,490 --> 00:15:06,660
Why Seung Ri's?

282
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:08,920
Well, Seung Ri's mom used to visit so often...

283
00:15:08,990 --> 00:15:10,390
she practically lived here,

284
00:15:10,530 --> 00:15:14,060
but she hasn't come by lately. I'm bored and a little curious.

285
00:15:14,430 --> 00:15:15,760
Okay, have a nice visit.

286
00:15:16,230 --> 00:15:18,500
She worked so hard from early in the morning...

287
00:15:18,570 --> 00:15:19,570
at the last event.

288
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:23,110
Tell her to stop by sometime. Say I'll make her a delicious lunch.

289
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:24,710
Okay, I'll be on my way.

290
00:15:24,770 --> 00:15:27,410
You two enjoy your time together, Father.

291
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:30,580
- All right, have a good trip. - Okay.

292
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:35,080
She may be immature and a bit flighty,

293
00:15:35,150 --> 00:15:38,850
but Min Ho's mom has a cute side to her.

294
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:43,930
Oh, of course. Oh, well, nobody is perfect.

295
00:15:44,830 --> 00:15:46,830
As long as she and Min Ho's dad are a good match,

296
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:47,900
that's all that matters.

297
00:15:49,570 --> 00:15:52,530
The problem is Min Ho's dad.

298
00:15:53,970 --> 00:15:54,970
Why?

299
00:15:55,840 --> 00:16:00,010
Is there some sort of problem with him these days?

300
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:06,120
How's Seung Ri, Mother?

301
00:16:06,250 --> 00:16:08,580
I don't know. She said she wants to be left alone,

302
00:16:08,650 --> 00:16:09,920
so I couldn't even get her to eat.

303
00:16:10,050 --> 00:16:13,660
- I'll go check on her. Don't worry. - Okay.

304
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:22,360
Seung Ri. I'm here.

305
00:16:23,930 --> 00:16:25,670
Are you really sick?

306
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:31,610
What's wrong? What hurts?

307
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:33,710
Wait.

308
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,750
Seung Ri, what's wrong with you?

309
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:44,050
What? You're burning up.

310
00:16:44,950 --> 00:16:48,190
- What? What is it? - Mother, she's burning up.

311
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:49,830
We have to get her to a hospital right away.

312
00:16:49,930 --> 00:16:53,060
What? She didn't have a fever at lunchtime.

313
00:16:53,130 --> 00:16:54,430
Oh my, Seung Ri.

314
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:57,370
One moment, Mother. Seung Ri, let's get you up.

315
00:16:57,430 --> 00:16:58,600
Let's go to the hospital.

316
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:00,940
Min Ho, please.

317
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,270
Just leave me alone.

318
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,370
I don't need to go to the hospital.

319
00:17:05,670 --> 00:17:08,810
What are you talking about? Your whole body is on fire.

320
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:11,910
Please, Min Ho.

321
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:15,520
Okay, fine.

322
00:17:16,550 --> 00:17:18,020
We won't go to the hospital,

323
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:20,120
but let's at least get this fever down, okay?

324
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,720
Mother, do you have any fever reducer here?

325
00:17:23,090 --> 00:17:25,730
And please bring me some ice water and a towel.

326
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:29,600
- Oh, okay. I'll get them. - Okay.

327
00:17:32,670 --> 00:17:35,600
What is wrong with you, Seo Seung Ri?

328
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:43,710
What brings you here?

329
00:17:44,410 --> 00:17:48,680
My gosh, you always ask what I want whenever I visit.

330
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:52,490
Can't I come see my best friend without having a reason?

331
00:17:52,850 --> 00:17:54,220
Please just go home for today.

332
00:17:54,890 --> 00:17:57,130
Seung Ri is home sick right now.

333
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,360
Oh, no, what's wrong with Seung Ri?

334
00:17:59,830 --> 00:18:03,070
Yes, she's sick. Very sick.

335
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:07,600
Why are you so harsh with me? Did I do something wrong?

336
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:09,440
I take it Min Ho's dad's face is just fine?

337
00:18:09,870 --> 00:18:11,710
He bruised Seung Ri's dad's face.

338
00:18:12,470 --> 00:18:14,110
What are you talking about?

339
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:16,080
Are you saying my husband...

340
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:18,110
and yours got into a fistfight?

341
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:21,080
And you pretended you didn't know anything about it.

342
00:18:22,450 --> 00:18:25,149
Mother, could you fill this with more ice?

343
00:18:25,150 --> 00:18:26,219
Okay.

344
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:28,020
I think the fever is starting to come down.

345
00:18:28,990 --> 00:18:29,990
Min Ho.

346
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:31,790
Mother.

347
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:33,460
What are you doing here?

348
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:36,530
I will explain later. Please do this for me.

349
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,200
Hey, Ko Min Ho.

350
00:18:39,170 --> 00:18:41,570
Did you leave work to come take care of Seung Ri?

351
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:43,640
What are you, her personal nurse?

352
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:44,940
Mother.

353
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,640
What is going on?

354
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:48,810
Look at the state of you.

355
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:51,210
Why are you here looking like this?

356
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:53,080
What is wrong with the way I look?

357
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:57,420
I do not want to fight with you right now, Mother.

358
00:18:58,450 --> 00:19:00,860
Oh my gosh, what is going on?

359
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:04,190
That brat. What a headache.

360
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:20,380
Where have you been?

361
00:19:20,710 --> 00:19:22,240
Were you at the Chairman's house this whole time?

362
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:24,610
No, it's not like that.

363
00:19:27,350 --> 00:19:31,250
Wait, what happened to your face? Don't tell me...

364
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:33,390
Did something happen with President Ko?

365
00:19:37,730 --> 00:19:39,590
Seo Gwon Sik, we need to talk.

366
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:42,400
For a long time now,

367
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:45,230
I've had my suspicions about many things.

368
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,840
And I have so many questions I want to ask.

369
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,640
Please, just be honest with me.

370
00:19:52,310 --> 00:19:54,840
Could that child from back then...

371
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,950
Yes, that's right.

372
00:20:01,820 --> 00:20:02,950
It's Team Leader Ko.

373
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:04,790
What?

374
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:09,320
Wait, how?

375
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:12,260
Han Su Cheol.

376
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:14,830
Team Leader Ko's biological father.

377
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,500
He was an employee on the design team...

378
00:20:18,130 --> 00:20:19,500
whom the Chairman cherished.

379
00:20:20,870 --> 00:20:22,170
After that accident,

380
00:20:22,670 --> 00:20:24,470
he found out Gyeol was at an orphanage.

381
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:26,940
After a long search, he found him,

382
00:20:27,710 --> 00:20:28,880
brought him home,

383
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:31,110
and had President Ko adopt him as his son.

384
00:20:31,950 --> 00:20:35,020
Of course, President Ko couldn't refuse.

385
00:20:38,290 --> 00:20:41,190
And I had no idea all this time...

386
00:20:45,690 --> 00:20:46,700
Sung Jun.

387
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:50,430
My daughter found out everything.

388
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:53,100
What?

389
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,900
What do you mean, she found out...

390
00:20:57,870 --> 00:20:59,170
That 25 years ago,

391
00:21:00,210 --> 00:21:01,710
the person who died in that accident...

392
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:04,450
was Team Leader Ko's father.

393
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:07,820
What?

394
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,320
I didn't care if anyone else knew,

395
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:15,290
but I never wanted my kids to know.

396
00:21:17,430 --> 00:21:18,930
Not my own children.

397
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,630
My daughter's whole world has been shattered.

398
00:21:28,270 --> 00:21:30,510
Team Leader Ko will find out soon enough...

399
00:21:33,310 --> 00:21:34,880
What am I supposed to do now?

400
00:21:38,950 --> 00:21:40,820
Do you think I can get through this, Sung Jun?

401
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:50,290
If only I had gotten my hands on that...

402
00:21:52,030 --> 00:21:53,060
If only...

403
00:21:56,530 --> 00:21:57,800
(100 Percent Korean Pork)

404
00:21:57,870 --> 00:21:59,229
- Here you go. - Thank you.

405
00:21:59,230 --> 00:22:00,640
- Thank you. - You're welcome. Enjoy.

406
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:03,970
- Now we need to get vegetables. - Right.

407
00:22:04,570 --> 00:22:06,810
- The vegetables are over there. - Oh, you're right.

408
00:22:07,910 --> 00:22:10,410
On our way, let's also grab some makgeolli that Mom likes.

409
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:12,550
Makgeolli? Your mother likes makgeolli?

410
00:22:12,610 --> 00:22:14,120
It's the only alcohol she drinks.

411
00:22:15,180 --> 00:22:18,850
- Some cabbage... - No, not that. This napa cabbage.

412
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,390
Oh, right. Napa cabbage is best for wraps.

413
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:23,120
What does your father like to drink?

414
00:22:23,190 --> 00:22:24,890
I'm going to have a drink with him today.

415
00:22:25,490 --> 00:22:28,100
Soju and beer. He can't drink a lot,

416
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,800
but he's not picky about what he drinks.

417
00:22:30,330 --> 00:22:31,970
- Did we forget anything? - I don't think so.

418
00:22:32,030 --> 00:22:34,670
You two look so lovely. You must be newlyweds.

419
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:36,470
Excuse me? Newlyweds?

420
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:38,440
Well, it's just...

421
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:44,350
That's right. We're newlyweds. I'm treating my in-laws to dinner,

422
00:22:44,810 --> 00:22:45,810
so could you pick out fresh cucumbers...

423
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:49,320
- and green peppers for me? - Oh, they're going to love you.

424
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:51,650
A son-in-law this nice and friendly.

425
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:54,990
Here.

426
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:58,290
Here, this is extra.

427
00:22:58,590 --> 00:23:00,860
It's on the house since you two are so cute together.

428
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:03,130
- Thank you. - Thank you.

429
00:23:07,370 --> 00:23:09,940
You two prepared all of this just for us?

430
00:23:10,970 --> 00:23:12,070
Where is everyone else?

431
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:14,880
Eun Hyung, Bit Na, and Eun Nim couldn't make it.

432
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:16,950
So we prepared something small and cosy for us.

433
00:23:17,510 --> 00:23:19,350
Bit Na said she missed her grandma,

434
00:23:19,410 --> 00:23:20,620
so she went over there today.

435
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,950
Mother, please have a drink.

436
00:23:24,490 --> 00:23:26,990
Oh, thank you.

437
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:29,990
Thank you. And I'm sorry.

438
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:32,260
What?

439
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:35,160
What do you have to be thankful and sorry to me for?

440
00:23:35,500 --> 00:23:39,270
Mother, we know what you gave up for our sake.

441
00:23:39,470 --> 00:23:43,970
Oh, not this again. How is that your fault?

442
00:23:44,870 --> 00:23:46,270
Whether or not my name is...

443
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:47,340
in the family register, she's still my mother.

444
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:49,810
I just didn't do it because it was too much trouble.

445
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:52,050
Mom, I am so sorry.

446
00:23:53,080 --> 00:23:54,820
Even if your name were registered,

447
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:57,890
I'm sure our relationship wouldn't change at all.

448
00:23:58,490 --> 00:24:01,920
I know you're doing this so we don't feel burdened,

449
00:24:01,990 --> 00:24:03,830
but can't you change your mind even now?

450
00:24:04,030 --> 00:24:05,760
Are you going to keep bringing up something that's already settled?

451
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:11,130
Team Leader Ko, if you feel sorry and grateful to me,

452
00:24:11,570 --> 00:24:13,400
you know what you have to do, right?

453
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:14,600
Yes, I know very well.

454
00:24:14,670 --> 00:24:16,470
To ensure your sacrifice is not in vain,

455
00:24:16,870 --> 00:24:20,980
we'll cherish and love each other and live happily to the very end.

456
00:24:25,780 --> 00:24:29,120
- Dad, have some more meat. - Okay. This looks delicious.

457
00:24:31,220 --> 00:24:33,660
- Here, let me pour you a drink. - Yes.

458
00:24:37,090 --> 00:24:39,760
No matter what happens,

459
00:24:40,930 --> 00:24:42,360
are you confident your feelings won't waver?

460
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:46,470
Of course. Whatever happens,

461
00:24:46,530 --> 00:24:48,800
we promised we'd never be apart.

462
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:50,970
Father, if you're worried...

463
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:53,270
about me going to the U.S., please don't be.

464
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:55,840
I will never leave Eun Ae alone.

465
00:24:56,380 --> 00:24:59,580
Does that mean you are giving up on going to the US?

466
00:25:01,020 --> 00:25:02,720
Yes, I might.

467
00:25:03,250 --> 00:25:05,490
If there is no other way, I can just go with him.

468
00:25:05,790 --> 00:25:08,820
I can still do whatever work I want to do over there.

469
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:11,160
So you love each other that much, is that it?

470
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:13,160
- Yes, of course. - Yes, of course.

471
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:17,330
- Father, let me pour you a drink. - Oh, sure.

472
00:25:19,630 --> 00:25:21,070
Here, you have a drink too.

473
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,440
Yes.

474
00:25:52,500 --> 00:25:54,540
(1985 Seoul High School)

475
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:15,960
(Jo Sung Jun, Seo Gwon Sik, Ko Dae Chi)

476
00:26:46,650 --> 00:26:47,660
Father.

477
00:27:18,220 --> 00:27:20,990
(Our Happy Days)

478
00:27:21,120 --> 00:27:24,589
Manager Seo found out, but only half the truth.

479
00:27:24,590 --> 00:27:27,499
- What? - Gwon Sik, if it still exists,

480
00:27:27,500 --> 00:27:29,330
what do you think you can do with it?

481
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,470
Do you have it by any chance?

482
00:27:31,530 --> 00:27:34,840
Don't you think it might cause an even bigger fallout?

483
00:27:34,940 --> 00:27:36,500
Then we weren't dating?

484
00:27:36,570 --> 00:27:40,940
- From a humanitarian standpoint... - Humanitarian? Seriously?

485
00:27:41,010 --> 00:27:42,040
What? Seung Ri?

486
00:27:42,110 --> 00:27:43,139
She said she was going to the hospital,

487
00:27:43,140 --> 00:27:44,980
but it has been over five hours and I cannot reach her.

488
00:27:45,250 --> 00:27:46,780
Where on earth could she have gone?

489
00:27:52,050 --> 00:27:54,920
(Our Happy Days)
